{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>A very great plague.</b> It happened, and the reason Moses did not pray on their behalf as he prayed at the plague of fire: it is possible to say that perhaps he was ashamed because of the great sin and the paucity of their faith in the Holy One, blessed be He, for they were ingrates; and they added transgression upon transgression — after they had complained when they went out into the wilderness, they lusted a lust, and did not take admonition from the first ones who were burned by fire. And further, he was ashamed because he had voiced complaint toward the Shekhinah and said, ״למה הרעות לעבדך״ — 'Why have You done ill to Your servant' — for he feared the attribute of Judgment that he mentioned above: ״ויחר אף ה׳ מאד״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:42.058252822Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}